On 24 January 2017 at 13:03, Eridk Poliruyt <ep1...@gmail.com> wrote:

> Thanks! The range was indeed too large. Would it help to extend the mesh (roughly twice the range?) ? Or it is not an ideal case for the SPDE model?

Well, model used (stationary field, no intercept) really isn't appropriate for the test data you had.
However, I notice that your test data was completely deterministic, which also doesn't play well with the observation likelihood, that includes random observation noise.  By changing the test case to

  z <- 20*sin((xy[,1]+xy[,2])/20) + rnorm(nrow(xy), 0.1)

the estimation becomes a lot more stable, and despite the estimated range baing a bit larger than the domain, the variance parameter estimates
actually does seem to scale in the way you intended, as well as the posterior predictions:

> signif(exp(rbind(
+   inla.spde.result(res1, "i", spde)$summary.log.range.nominal[quant],
+   inla.spde.result(res2, "i", spde)$summary.log.range.nominal[quant],
+   inla.spde.result(res3, "i", spde)$summary.log.range.nominal[quant],
+   inla.spde.result(res1, "i", spde)$summary.log.variance.nominal[quant],
+   inla.spde.result(res2, "i", spde)$summary.log.variance.nominal[quant]+2*log(20),
+   inla.spde.result(res3, "i", spde)$summary.log.variance.nominal[quant]-2*log(20))),
+   digits=3)
                    0.025quant 0.5quant 0.975quant
range.nominal.1         1.3200    2.860       6.47
range.nominal.11        1.3300    3.240       7.20
range.nominal.12        1.3800    2.960       6.48
variance.nominal.1      0.1080    0.350       1.58
variance.nominal.11     0.0945    0.382       1.82
variance.nominal.12     0.1030    0.336       1.60

> summary(z)
   Min. 1st Qu.  Median    Mean 3rd Qu.    Max.

-1.5430  0.4533  1.1260  1.1620  1.8230  4.0870

> summary(apply(zm1,1,mean))
   Min. 1st Qu.  Median    Mean 3rd Qu.    Max.

 0.5705  0.8478  1.1170  1.1570  1.4640  1.8680

> summary(apply(zm2*20,1,mean))
   Min. 1st Qu.  Median    Mean 3rd Qu.    Max.

 0.5769  0.8540  1.1170  1.1600  1.4660  1.8870

> summary(apply(zm3/20,1,mean))
   Min. 1st Qu.  Median    Mean 3rd Qu.    Max.

 0.5724  0.8470  1.1210  1.1580  1.4660  1.8620

> summary(apply(zm1,1,sd))
   Min. 1st Qu.  Median    Mean 3rd Qu.    Max.

 0.1047  0.1174  0.1267  0.1336  0.1455  0.2181

> summary(apply(zm2*20,1,sd))
   Min. 1st Qu.  Median    Mean 3rd Qu.    Max.

 0.1072  0.1143  0.1232  0.1311  0.1434  0.2183

> summary(apply(zm3/20,1,sd))
   Min. 1st Qu.  Median    Mean 3rd Qu.    Max.

 0.1007  0.1127  0.1232  0.1294  0.1431  0.2141

