The likelihood? Not the formula. What "inla()" calls the "family".

When it comes to the number of parameters, that can mean many different things. The estimated effective number of parameters from INLA is not the one I was thinking of.

If you want to compare any model to a complex model, my understanding is that DIC is not adequate. But again, I have no proof.

You: "Also, does this model not compute a slope and intercept for random effects?"
I do not understand this question.

Haakon

